  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that RNA-only scvi_n200 with multiprofile aggregation is much better than PCA or scGPT, with config_006 and config_005 both around 0.65 validation accuracy and F1. Image-only resnet50 is weak, so the key uncertainty is whether adding image features to the best RNA setup can improve performance. config_032 keeps the best RNA encoder, profile setting, and aggregation fixed while adding resnet50 image features with simple concat fusion. This directly tests the marginal value of the image modality without confounding the result with an untested ViT-L encoder or weighted fusion, making it a focused exploitation of the strongest RNA evidence and a clean baseline for later fusion or image-encoder comparisons."
}

